{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975791,"nonce":"gspoUMoetsUUL4lX82DFvUSrC5U=","title":"Generate the reflection call bridge with Cranelift instead of hand-written assembly","message":"`ash_static_call` is per-ABI assembly (aarch64 and x86_64, with no fallback, so an\nunported architecture fails to link) that marshals arguments into registers for a\nsignature known only at runtime. It is reached as a function pointer installed\nthrough `hl_setup_callbacks2`, so it can be a trampoline emitted per distinct\nsignature by the Cranelift backend already in the tree and cached by signature.\nArchitecture support would then follow the backends.\n\nThe fiber context switch cannot be handled this way: swapping the stack pointer\nand restoring callee-saved registers is inexpressible in both LLVM IR and CLIF,\nwhich assume call/return discipline.","files":null}]}